  "warnings": [
   "Google 'Store visits' is MISSING entirely for the current week (W36, 2026-09-07) in ALL THREE accounts - no row is returned for that action. Store visits is a modelled metric that lands with a lag, so the W36 walkin figures (Aqua NYC 131, Hutong NYC 335.93, Hutong Miami 75) are understated and NOT comparable with prior weeks or LY. This is the same pattern seen last week: last week's file recorded Hutong NYC W35 walkin as 286.17; refetched now it is 477.37 (+67%) once Store visits (64.7) and a restated Click Book Now landed. Treat W36 walkin as provisional.",
   "Current-year Google walkin figures for W33-W35 have been restated upward vs last week's file (Hutong NYC W33 660.26 -> 676.16, W34 563.80 -> 580.70) because modelled Store visits keep accruing. LY (L33-L35) values reconcile exactly to last week's file, confirming the restatement is confined to recent weeks.",
   "Small Google restatements on the overlapping week: Hutong NYC W35 spend 1160.38 -> 1160.64 and booking conv 18.952694 -> 19.952694; W32 conv 53.307347 -> 57.307347. Meta Hutong NYC W35 spend 808.80 -> 809.20. All refreshed values used here.",
   "Hutong NYC Meta has only TWO campaigns with delivery in the current week (Conversions and Awareness | Video Viewers), so the 'top 3' list has two entries. 'CRKLR | NEW Retargeting Campaign' spent in prior weeks but had zero impressions this week - a legitimate zero (campaign off), not a data gap.",
   "Zero-bookings entries that are legitimate, not missing data: Hutong NYC Meta 'Awareness | Video Viewers' (0 schedules - a video-view objective campaign, no pixel Schedule events), Hutong Miami Meta 'Awareness - LPV Campaign' (0), Hutong NYC Google 'Demand Gen > Generic' (0 booking conversions), Hutong Miami Google 'P. Max > Generic' and 'Search > Special Events' (0 each; Miami booked only via 'Search > Chinese Cuisine' 6 and 'Search > Brand' 1 this week).",
   "Hutong Miami Google uses 'Calls from ads (1)' (with a trailing ' (1)') and a lowercase 'Click to email', where Hutong NYC uses 'Calls from ads' and 'Click To Email'. None of these are in the walkin rule so totals are unaffected, but the naming is inconsistent across accounts and worth cleaning up in Google Ads.",
   "Aqua NYC Google has no 'Click Book Now' conversion action at all, so its walkin is Store visits + Directions + Menu views + Clicks to call only, and is structurally lower than the Hutong accounts. Not comparable venue-to-venue.",
   "Aqua NYC Google spend has roughly halved since W30 (1134.67 -> 693.44) with booking conversions down from 52.0 to 23.0; consistent with the known CRKLR budget-reset behaviour on this account. No data issue, flagged for interpretation.",
